T3  Derivative identity, and the detached-gradient control
==============================================================================
  ||Phi^T dG/d eta||                     = 4.489780e-02   (no projection)
  ||Phi^T dG_tilde/d eta||, through      = 2.020614e-13   ratio to raw = 4.500e-12
  ||Phi^T dG_tilde/d eta||, detached     = 4.489780e-02   ratio to raw = 1.000e+00
  ||dG_tilde/d eta - (I - P) dG/d eta||  = 3.875e-17 (Prop. 5.2 of the derivation)
  VERDICT: differentiating THROUGH the coefficient is required. Detaching it leaves the Jacobian non-orthogonal at the same magnitude as no projection.

